{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Joseph is a fruitful vine.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the word בן is from the expression (Psalms 80:16) ״ועל בן אמצת לך״, and its meaning is a planting that has many fruits, and this is an allusion to the two tribes that come forth from him, Ephraim and Manasseh; and because of this he mentioned בן פרת twice, and this is why Moses likened him to an ox and a ראם, and explained, saying (Deuteronomy 33:17): ״והם רבבות אפרים והם אלפי מנשה״. And the reason he prefaced the praise with the name Joseph and did not do so with the rest of the tribes, is that he needed to duplicate בן פרת twice, corresponding to the two tribes, and it would not be possible to write יוסף בן פרת בן פרת עלי עין. Therefore he needed to preface the praise before the name Joseph, and said: פרת יוסף בן פרת עלי עין. And the first בן פרת corresponds to Manasseh the firstborn, and the second בן פרת corresponds to Ephraim; and since his superiority was great over Manasseh, he added עלי עין." "<b>And the Ramban</b>, of blessed memory, explained בן פרת as בן חן — 'a son of grace' — from the language of our Rabbis of blessed memory: 'אפריון נמטייה לר׳ שמעון' at the end of Bava Metzi'a, and likewise the language of ברכה ושבח from the expression פורנא ליתמי. Thus far." "<b>Daughters tread upon.</b> The daughters of the kings in Egypt would go up and tread upon the walls of the city in order to gaze at him, and he did not set his eyes on any one of them; therefore it is joined to him: ״ותשב באיתן קשתו״. <br><b>By way of the Midrash:</b> בן פרת בן פרות — through cows he was raised. <br><b>עלי עין:</b> do not read עלי עין but rather עולי עין — they rise upon the eye — this is the seed of Joseph, over whom the evil eye has no dominion." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> בן פרת alludes to תפארת ישראל, and this is the meaning of בן פרת; and the sense of עלי עין is that it — Tiferet — is upon the river that goes forth from Eden, flowing upon the river and bestowing upon it. And because נצח is from the right and הוד from the left, therefore two tribes came forth from him, Ephraim and Manasseh. And this is what is meant by <b>בנות צעדה עלי שור</b>, which Onkelos translated: ״תרין שבטין יפקון מבנוהי״ — 'two tribes shall come forth from his sons.' And from this Moses mentioned in his blessing (Deuteronomy 33:17): ״בכור שורו הדר לו״ — he came to explain the two attributes given to Joseph: the שור from the left, and the הודר, which is the נצח, from the right. And this is clear."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "The text reads פרת יוסף without the word בן in the second clause; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:50.924194028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}